# Security audit working notes. Deliberately untracked: this repository is
# public, and the report enumerates findings that are still OPEN against the
# live deployment (retention/authz on the originals store, digest escaping,
# output sanitization) along with the steps to reach them. Publishing that is
# publishing a target list. Track open findings in private GitHub Security
# Advisories instead, and commit the report — or the closed part of it — once
# the findings it describes are actually fixed.
SECURITY-AUDIT.md

# Binary fixtures are generated on demand (fixtures/scripts/make_binary_fixtures.py).
# The repo stays text-only.
fixtures/_generated/

# DSPy optimization artifacts are machine-generated per run.
eval/artifacts/

# Agent skills installed by `npx skills add` — vendored third-party content that
# goes stale. `skills-lock.json` IS tracked (it records source + content hash),
# so the set is reproducible the same way node_modules is: ignore the install,
# commit the lockfile.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
